R-IX6 R-IX4 R-AP74 R-SO13 R-DI12 (slice 206d2, Design Q467): `tln update --no-check --dry-run --offline` with a registry (config.toml) and `[toolchain] roc = ">=nightly-2026-10-10-0000000"`, no compiler installed or on PATH, so the range step must choose a compiler (R-SO13, also with --no-check). Offline, the compiler list is the kept rows of toolchains.json at any age (R-IX4, R-IX6); there is no copy, so the list is empty, and R-AP74 row 4 gives the first cause: exit 10 (`no_tuple`), `no compiler is left: the compiler list of the registry is empty` (the text of `ClosureRequest.no_compiler`, slice 205b, a proposal). Not the exit 15 of `direct` (`no cached list of compilers`). No request, no write except projects.json.
Changed by Design Q489 (slice 206e2 round 2): an offline run with no toolchains.json has a list that cannot be read, not an empty list (R-AP74 row 4, R-IX6). The rule of direct applies: a command with no held compiler fails with the failure of the list, `Toolchain.offline_no_list` (exit 15, `no cached list of compilers and --offline is set`). The calls and the tree do not change.
